## 2. Exact geometric mechanism

Let the permanent-Record set initially be

```text
R(f,L) = {-2f} union {0,f,2f,...,(L-1)f},    L >= 2.
```

For an empty candidate `x`, the frozen predicate requires exactly one nearest
Record `p`, infers `d=x-p`, requires another Record at `x-2d`, and requires the
other five nearest neighbors to be empty.

There is a short graph proof.  The trail Records form one adjacency path and
the cap is isolated.  Every eligible candidate must extrapolate a directed
adjacent Record edge.  The only empty extrapolations of the trail path are
`-f` and `Lf`.  Candidate `-f` has two nearest Records, at `-2f` and `0`, so it
fails the unique-neighbor test.  Candidate `Lf` has the unique predecessor
`(L-1)f` and grand-predecessor `(L-2)f`, so it passes.  A lateral neighbor of
the cap has no collinear grand-predecessor, and `-3f` likewise lacks one at
`-f`.

Proper cubic rotations and translations preserve adjacency, the empty gap,
and the relation `cap=-2f`.  Hence

```text
E(QR+t) = {(Qx+t,Qd) : (x,d) in E(R)}.
```

The primary runner checks all six signed fronts, all 24 proper cubic frames,
and 42 translated cases in exact integer geometry.

## 3. Complete finite-frontier census

The primary census covers six fronts, sixteen lengths from two through
seventeen, and 84 possible hidden registered cap-content assignments:

```text
6 x 16 x 84 = 8,064 capped trail/content controls.
```

Across 362,880 complete-frontier candidate evaluations, each control has
exactly one forward tip.  The 84 content assignments intentionally repeat the
same flag geometry: their purpose is to demonstrate observational invariance,
not to inflate the number of distinct shapes.  The public predicate receives
only the Record-flag set, while an AST/runtime-interface certificate excludes
Record content, a codebook, cap metadata, host direction, site identity, role,
epoch, scheduler, target fixture, and same-event outcome feedback.

Finite-prefix induction is exact.  Adding the accepted forward Record maps
`R(f,L)` to `R(f,L+1)` while leaving the cap and gap unchanged, so the same
one-tip argument applies to every later finite prefix, conditional on clear
transport and the supplied initial capped seed.

## 4. Controller and local STOP

The cap is Manhattan distance two behind the seed and is disjoint from all ten
source/destination footprint sites of the earliest legal event; separation
only grows for later events.  The frozen composed census covers

```text
6 fronts x 14 predecessor outcomes x 14 new outcomes x 32 obstacle masks
= 37,632 guarded maps.
```

All 1,176 clear maps make the exact successor.  All 36,456 blocked maps are
identity on every source and destination, preserve all occupied Records, move
no partial packet, and add no packet cells.  The unchanged fourteen-way law
plus local STOP is normalized in all 2,688 declared distributions and the
guard is outcome-independent.

The stronger restart test covers all 31 nonempty obstacle masks, six fronts,
and all sixteen lengths: 2,976 blocked cap/trail/new-Record/obstacle
components.  It evaluates the complete empty frontier in 171,936 candidate
checks.  The only forward trail extrapolation is blocked by at least one
occupied controller destination; the cap continues to block the rear gap; and
isolated obstacle sites create no valid collinear predecessor pair.  Maximum
eligible count is zero.

This is local STOP for the declared finite component, not a claim that the
whole lattice is absorbing.  An unrelated or overlapping front may still act.

## 5. What the result buys

Block 14 showed that the existing nonorthogonal Record contents contain enough
classical information to orient an effective history, but it left the physical
readout functional and its microscopic implementation open.  Block 15 shows a
cheaper conditional route: store the direction once in the geometry of a
permanent cap, then propagate using flags alone.  Repeated nonorthogonal
content discrimination is no longer needed by the effective front rule.

That is a meaningful bridge advance.  It says the propagation architecture is
compatible with a very small arrow carrier, and it gives a crisp target for a
microscopic writer.  It is not yet formal TOE progress because the arrow has
been moved into boundary data rather than derived.

The cap's hidden content may be arbitrary, but exact flag sensing is still an
effective framework operation.  This block constructs neither the microscopic
instrument that distinguishes Record/no-Record sectors nor a finite-depth
realization of the atomic five-site AND/broadcast controller.

