## 7. Why the cap is supplied

The input state already distinguishes `f` from `-f`: the isolated cap marks
the rear endpoint at distance two.  Nothing in the current event creates that
marker.  This is the literal meaning of `supplied_cap: true` and
`generated_cap: false`; it is not an impossibility statement.

There is one narrow symmetry observation.  A deterministic equivariant map
from an exactly cubic-invariant precursor to one nonzero signed axis cannot
exist, because the output would have to be fixed by every proper cubic
rotation.  This does not block stochastic symmetry breaking.  A covariant
instrument may produce six equiprobable signed-axis branches, or a 24-branch
frame orbit, and let the realized Record branch carry the arrow.

That writer must create the cap and the live packet together without receiving
`f`, a chosen site, role, epoch, tape, or scheduler.  If it succeeds, the
supplied-boundary import can be tested for retirement.  If it fails, the exact
failure—not the present positive—will determine whether the residual belongs
to dynamics, boundary conditions, or the axioms.

## 8. Portfolio implication

Repeating more supplied-cap lengths has low leverage after the complete
frontier and blocked-component certificates.  The highest-value successor is
the covariant generated cap-plus-live-packet writer.  It should be co-designed
with an explicit overlapping-event conflict channel or finite-depth local
instrument, because a writer that works only in isolation merely moves the
next wall one step downstream.

An orthogonal distributed direction pointer remains the fallback if exact
flag sensing or the cap footprint cannot be realized microscopically.  Rate
and time should follow only after a well-defined concurrent transition exists.
Connection and gravity remain essential TOE obligations, but another
conditional finite response calculation will not retire their supplied
action, temporal, source, and conservation inputs.

The minimal axioms should remain unchanged now.  The next campaign is designed
to decide whether existing Admissibility plus Record resources can generate
the arrow carrier; only a precise exhausted residual would justify proposing
an axiom-level change.
